# v1.23.5 — cache policy. THE chronic "live lags the zip" fix: pages must
# REVALIDATE on every open (no-cache = cheap 304 when unchanged, fresh HTML
# the moment a deploy lands), while hashed build files never need rechecking.
# Without this, phones held old builds long after every DEPLOY.bat.
#
# v1.26.3 (CEO: "I still encounter location for the android phone"): the
# Permissions-Policy below WAS the Android mystery. geolocation=() told
# browsers to forbid the Geolocation API for the whole site — Android
# Chrome/Samsung Internet enforce it (instant "denied" no matter what the
# user allows), while iPhone Safari ignores this directive, which is why
# only Androids were "blocked". It shipped with this very file in v1.23.5 —
# exactly when the Android complaints began. geolocation=(self): our own
# pages may ask; embedded third-party frames still cannot. Camera/mic stay
# locked (nothing in the system uses them).
#
# v1.45.0 (security audit C1) — CSP and HSTS join, at last.
# The portal is the more sensitive of the two systems (staff sessions, HR,
# payroll, the signed-document vault) and was shipping WEAKER headers than
# the storefront: no Content-Security-Policy at all, and no HSTS. Each
# directive below is chosen against what this app actually loads, so nothing
# breaks:
#   script-src  'self' + 'unsafe-inline' — Next inlines its hydration
#               bootstrap into every statically exported page, and a static
#               export cannot mint a per-request nonce. cloudflareinsights is
#               the analytics beacon in app/layout.tsx.
#   style-src   'unsafe-inline' — Tailwind and React set inline styles.
#   img-src     https: — product, staff and client logos come from R2 through
#               our own /api, but brand logos are also linked from client
#               sites; data:/blob: cover generated PDFs and QR codes.
#   frame-src   'self' blob: data: for the document preview (an iframe with
#               srcDoc + generated PDFs), google.com for the office map on
#               /contact.
#   connect-src 'self' + the beacon endpoint. The API is same-origin.
#   frame-ancestors 'none' — with X-Frame-Options: DENY, this portal can
#               never be framed. That is how a fake login is built on top of
#               a real one.
#   object-src 'none' — nothing here embeds a plugin document.
# HSTS: one year, subdomains included. Every route is https already; this
# closes the first-request downgrade window.
#
# v1.71.0 (Track V) - /cards/*.vcf must be served as text/vcard. Cloudflare
# Pages has no mapping for the extension and falls back to octet-stream,
# which some phones save as a file instead of opening the contact card. The
# whole point of the feature is the "Add to contacts" sheet appearing.
# Immutable is deliberately NOT set on them: a vCard is small, and a stale
# phone number cached for a year is exactly the failure this feature exists
# to prevent.
#
# NOTE: comments live ONLY here at the top — a # line inside a rule block
# can be misparsed as a header. tests/permissions-policy.mjs guards this.
/*
  X-Content-Type-Options: nosniff
  X-Frame-Options: DENY
  Referrer-Policy: strict-origin-when-cross-origin
  Permissions-Policy: camera=(), microphone=(), geolocation=(self)
  Strict-Transport-Security: max-age=31536000; includeSubDomains
  Content-Security-Policy: default-src 'self'; script-src 'self' 'unsafe-inline' https://static.cloudflareinsights.com; style-src 'self' 'unsafe-inline'; img-src 'self' data: blob: https:; font-src 'self' data:; connect-src 'self' https://static.cloudflareinsights.com; frame-src 'self' blob: data: https://www.google.com; media-src 'self' blob:; form-action 'self'; base-uri 'self'; object-src 'none'; frame-ancestors 'none'; upgrade-insecure-requests
  Cache-Control: no-cache

/_next/static/*
  Cache-Control: public, max-age=31536000, immutable

/cards/*.vcf
  Content-Type: text/vcard; charset=utf-8
